A||N||10||Elenor84||Guages Go wacky then stall????????||||8||
Z||000000||Elenor84||10-02-2001||02:20 PM||||Hey guys...the other day I was driving and I got into third gear and all of a sudden there was a clunk and all my guages went wacky bouncing up and down like nuts...then it stalled...I pulled over and sorrta messed around with wires and minor stuff...then it fired perfect and didn't have another problem until today when the exact same thing happened...this time when I turned the key one click forward the lights didn't even come on in the dash...but after a while they flickered and finally came on and then she fired...whats goin on with my engine?  Electrical?  Where?<BR>thx guys!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||8
Z||000001||Voytek||10-02-2001||02:34 PM||||You may have a short from the battery somewhere.  I've had the hot wire from the battery touching the engine - it wore through and started doing a similar thing, i.e. everytime it sparked, it would jerk the car and all of the gauges went really funny.  Check the hot and ground wires from your alt. to battery and from battery to starter.<P>That's all I can think of.<P>If it just died while driving, no sound and no funny stuff, I'd guess the control module in the distributor.  They tend to die when engine hot and run againg when it cools off.<P>Have you ran the code tester?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Elenor84||10-02-2001||03:10 PM||||Voytek...no check engine light came on when this happended...would it still be in the memory?  If so I will test it...and I'll check those connections..thx!<BR>How was the drive home on sunday?<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-02-2001||03:45 PM||||check the fuses, make sure there are no loose ones ,perhaps clean/tighten your battery cables, and maybe check for any bare spots (frame rubbing?) on your battery cables causing it to short out..<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||kinboyatuwo||10-02-2001||05:03 PM||||DFor sure that is the problem, there is a power and ground contact short.  Had this problem last year, mine was the ground strap for the trunk lid had frayed and was touching the power wire<BR>finding it might be the hard part<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/b4lower50.jpg"> <BR>"Friends don't let friends drive four doors."<P>87 Duke, 235,000km||||reg||4
Z||000005||Voytek||10-02-2001||05:31 PM||||If the check engine light came on by itself, PRIOR to the car dying, there could be a code stored in the memory - ONLY if it's a sensor that caused this.<P>More than likely, though, it'll be a short (like Kinboyatuwo said) in the power wiring somewhere, most likely from the battery.<P>Fuses are a possibility but only if something is shorting out in the fuse box.  No single fuse will cause everything in your car to go haywire.  Like I said, UNLESS there is a short somewhere WITHIN the fuse box - you should be able to tell, just unscrew the fuse box and look for something fried on the back of it.<P>Good luck.<P>Hey, I didn't even realize you were from Edmonton.  Cool.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Elenor84||10-02-2001||08:36 PM||||Ya man...I was the blond haired punk...<P>anyways thx alot for all your help guys!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||johnt671||10-03-2001||05:59 PM||||Had that problem several times on my 84.  Always turned out to be one or more of the wires running down to the starter shorting out.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Elenor84||10-08-2001||08:05 PM||||I know I posted a new one but I have to add to this...all these problems it may be but the main thing is that when I open my door my interior lights come on...which is normal....but when I turn the key one forward the dash lights don't come on...wouldn't they still come on since the interior lights come on or are the 2 seperate things?  <BR>Thx guys...I guess its time to get really dirty and find this short...||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fierowrecker||10-08-2001||08:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Elenor84:<BR><B>Hey guys...the other day I was driving and I got into third gear and all of a sudden there was a clunk and all my guages went wacky bouncing up and down like nuts...then it stalled...I pulled over and sorrta messed around with wires and minor stuff...then it fired perfect and didn't have another problem until today when the exact same thing happened...this time when I turned the key one click forward the lights didn't even come on in the dash...but after a while they flickered and finally came on and then she fired...whats goin on with my engine?  Electrical?  Where?<BR>thx guys!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Elenor!<BR>I had the same problem on my 84!<BR>The wire ran from the alternator down and around the pulley side of the engine behind a plastic cover...<BR>There was a factory splice to add a second wire to the line, and the insulating tape unwrapped allowing the metal splice to short out against the block...<BR>Good luck on the hunt!<BR><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">        <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Elenor84||10-08-2001||08:17 PM||||Hey fierowrecker...thx man...give me 30min and I'll reply back with whatever I find...here we go!!!!!||||reg||1
